body:
Let V,W be vector spaces over F and let B be a basis of V . Suppose
g ∶B Ð→W is a function, and let f ∶V Ð→W be its extension to V by linearity.
Prove that
(a) f is injective if and only if g(B) is linearly independent in W;
(b) f is surjective if and only if g(B) spans W;
(c) f is bijective if and only if g(B) is a basis for W.

